# FlowSchedule — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
# The path is resolved relative to prisma/schema.prisma (src/lib/db-path.ts).

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and
# the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract.)
#
# Session 9 (db-path v3): this file — the REPO'S OWN .env — is AUTHORITATIVE
# for DATABASE_URL. An ambient environment variable carrying a SQLite
# file: URL that resolves OUTSIDE the repo is ignored (parent-workspace
# .env hijack protection — Bun auto-loads parent .env files, and CI
# harnesses can export DATABASE_URL into the shell; both were real-world
# repros). Two deliberate exceptions keep winning over this file:
#   - an ambient SQLite URL that resolves INSIDE the repo (the e2e
#     suite's file:../db/e2e.db isolation override), and
#   - a non-SQLite ambient URL (PostgreSQL in production).
# The CLI-facing db scripts (db:push/db:migrate/db:reset) apply the same
# rule via scripts/prisma-cli.ts; db:seed self-resolves.
#
# For production, either set an ABSOLUTE path HERE, or remove/comment the
# DATABASE_URL line and set the environment variable — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string (env var or here)
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — feeds metadataBase, sitemap.xml and robots.txt
# via src/lib/site.ts (falls back to http://localhost:3000 when unset).
# Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth (src/lib/auth.ts).
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""
